      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. To be more specific, I'm dealing with cases where the lesions have a very strange, almost malformed or \"gnarled\" appearance that doesn't match standard dermatological textbook descriptions. In these instances where the physical morphology is particularly irregular or looks \"off\" compared to healthy tissue, is there a specific hierarchy I should follow to differentiate between a simple benign irregularity and something that might require a more complex diagnostic code? I want to make sure we aren't under-coding these anomalous presentations.",
